Z||000000||wkayl||02-15-2000||11:42 PM||||I hear all the talk about modifications and new paint on cars.  How many out there have cars in as near original as possible.  The Indy pace car on FieroDave's site is one example.  My car now has 82,000 miles and is original except for sunroof put in by a previous owner.  Radio display didn't work, so I have put in aftermarket for now untill I get enough play money to repair the old one.  Rear wing is a little faded otherwise paint shines like new (few rock chips and scratches).  Engine compartment and front compartment very clean.  Interior I would rate an 8 out of 10 (but that is just my opinion).  I would like to hear from others (bragging is accepted).  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/001170.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/001170.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||02-16-2000||08:48 AM||||Your car's so pretty it makes my heart hurt, especially that shot of the open decklid.  It looks brand new.  I want another V6 so bad it keeps me awake at night.<P>For the record, my 88 Coupe is all original at 106K miles with the exception of KYB shocks/struts, Formula rear springs and a new NAPA clutch at 71K miles.  It does have an aftermarket sunroof, but that was installed by the dealer before the original owner took delivery.||||reg||1
