Z||000039||mrfixit58||02-24-2000||11:56 AM||||Ok, Ok,... With all this talk about original Fieros (and because I've got a new digital camera) I thought I'd show you mine... er.. Fiero, that is...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierolft.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroint2.jpg"> <P>This is the car that I had for sale a few months ago and got no takers (or even offers). So, I decided to keep it and keep collecting parts to fix it up.<P>I've since fixed the steering column wobble, found replacement seat covers, a working A/C, compressor, an original wing and various little parts to finish it off. The only problem with the body is the paint. The car had a bra on it's nose for it's hole life and the paint and nose piece are in great shape (but only there). As you can se from the picture, the dash is perfect as is most of everything else except for the seat covers and headliner. Except for some aftermarket alarm system, this car is original.<P>I probably won't get to her for about another year (I have to finish my 68 RS Camaro first). after I sell the Camaro, this baby will probably get a 3800 SC motor.<P>enjoy!<P>RoyL.||||reg||12
